course: dictionary
lesson: 12381
title: Cubical: shaped like a cube
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cubical means shaped like a cube. A cube has six faces, and every face is an equal square. The word comes from cube, so think of a dice or a sugar cube. «The gift box was cubical, with six square sides.» The clue is square sides, which tells you the box looks like a cube.
explain: Use the swap test. Put cube-shaped in place of cubical: «The gift box was cube-shaped, with six square sides.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. People often say cube-shaped in everyday talk, and cubical is the more formal word.
explain: In maths, a cubical box has the same length, width and height. To find its volume, multiply side × side × side. «The cubical tank had sides of 2 metres.» Each side is 2 metres, so the volume is 2 × 2 × 2 = 8 cubic metres.
fact: Cubical means shaped like a cube, with six equal square faces.
fact: Cubical is a formal word; in everyday talk people often say cube-shaped.
fact: «Cubical» comes from the word cube, so a cube is a good picture to remember.
fact: In maths, a cubical box has the same length, width and height.
fact: In science, salt crystals are often cubical in shape.
exercise: «The gift box was cubical, with six square sides.» What does cubical mean? | Flat like a pancake | Long and thin like a pencil | *Shaped like a cube | Round like a ball
exercise: Mia says the salt crystals look cubical under the microscope. What shape is she describing? | A long tube | *A cube with six equal square faces | A ball | A triangle
exercise: «A cubical box has the same length, width and height.» Which box is cubical? | *A box 4 cm long, 4 cm wide and 4 cm high | A box with only three square sides | A box 5 cm long, 2 cm wide and 9 cm high | A box with round sides
test: «The cubical tank had sides of 2 metres.» What is the volume of the tank? | 12 cubic metres | *8 cubic metres | 6 cubic metres | 4 cubic metres
test: Which word means nearly the same as cubical in everyday talk? | Heavy | Round | Sticky | *Cube-shaped
exam: Which sentence uses cubical correctly? | Her cubical voice was loud | The river was cubical | *The ice tray had cubical compartments | The ball was cubical
